  "seoBody": "<section><span class=\"eyebrow\">Quickler in Canada</span><p>Canadian field firms already coordinate crews over WhatsApp. Quickler turns that same channel into inspections, checklists and certificates. A worker on a site in Toronto, Calgary or Halifax answers questions by text, voice note or photo, and every answer becomes a clean, structured digital record on a manager dashboard, with red, amber and green fault status. When a formal document is needed, a PDF exports straight from that record. No app to install, and you only pay for active users, no hardware to ship across the provinces.</p></section><h2>A structured digital record, not just a piece of paper.</h2><p>Most field tools leave a manager with a stack of PDFs to read one by one. Quickler leads with something more useful: a live, machine-readable record of every job, sortable and searchable on one dashboard.</p><ul><li>Every inspection lands on the dashboard with red, amber and green fault status</li><li>Managers see what failed, where, and who recorded it without opening a file</li><li>Photos and voice notes attach to the exact question they answer</li><li>A PDF exports from the record whenever a client, insurer or regulator wants a document</li></ul><p>For a Canadian firm running checks across multiple sites and time zones, that shift from a pile of documents to one structured record is the practical difference.</p><h2>Crews use the WhatsApp account already on their phone.</h2><p>Field work in Canada often means subcontractors, seasonal crews and bilingual teams who change from job to job. Asking each of them to download, log in to and learn a new app is where adoption stalls.</p><ul><li>The field worker opens WhatsApp, which they already use every day</li><li>There is nothing to install, no account to create, no password to reset on site</li><li>It works the same on any Canadian carrier and on any phone</li><li>Because dormant users are free, adding a casual crew member costs nothing</li></ul><p>The barrier to getting a worker recording proper compliance data drops to one message.</p><h2>Any inspection a Canadian field firm runs.</h2><h3>Electrical, gas, plumbing and HVAC</h3><p>Upload your own inspection sheet and quickler builds it into a guided WhatsApp workflow. Condition ratings, defect logging, photos and sign-off carry through to the structured record, whatever the trade.</p><h3>Construction, fire safety and facilities checks</h3><p>Site safety walks, fire and equipment inspections, and routine facilities checks all run the same way. The dashboard keeps a running picture of every location's status across a large or spread-out portfolio.</p><h3>Vehicle walkrounds and remote crews</h3><p>Fleet walkround checks and lone-worker records suit WhatsApp well, because a driver or remote worker can complete them from anywhere with a signal. Canada's distances make that reach matter.</p><h2>Running Quickler in Canada.</h2><h3>Do my crews need to install anything?</h3><p>No. They answer in WhatsApp on the phone they already use. There is nothing to download and only pay for active users.</p><h3>What do I actually get back?</h3><p>A structured digital record on a manager dashboard with red, amber and green fault status. A PDF exports from it whenever you need a formal document.</p><h3>Can it run my own Canadian forms?</h3><p>Yes. Quickler is job-agnostic. Upload any inspection or checklist form and quickler builds it into a WhatsApp workflow.</p><h3>Where does my data sit?</h3><p>On EU servers in Germany, with a GDPR-aligned design. It is a privacy-respecting base independent of any single app store or carrier.</p><h3>What does it cost?</h3><p>Pricing is quoted in GBP, with EUR and USD available on request. There is dormant users free, so cost does not climb with crew size.</p><h3>How do I start?</h3><p>Read how the product works <a href=\"/pages/global-field-compliance.html\">across any country</a>, browse the <a href=\"/pages/services.html\">workflows</a>, or <a href=\"/pages/help/index.html#contact-form-section\">get in touch</a> to shape one for your firm.</p>",
